/a><sup>(×2)</sup> + 7 times <a data-ref=\"Numbers 3\" href=\"/Numbers.3\">Nu 3</a> (P); with certain perquisites <a data-ref=\"Numbers 18:24\" href=\"/Numbers.18.24\">Nu 18:24</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 18:26\" href=\"/Numbers.18.26\">26</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 18:30\" href=\"/Numbers.18.30\">30</a> + 9 times Nu (P). <strong>B.</strong>  in Chr. the tribal idea is in the background, and thought of Levites as official class is prominent: <strong>a.</strong>  disting. from priests <span dir=\"rtl\">הַכּ׳ וְהַל׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 9:14\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.9.14\">1 Ch 9:14</a> (cf. v <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 9:10\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.9.10\">10</a>), <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 13:2\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.13.2\">13:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 15:4\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.15.4\">15:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 15:11\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.15.11\">11</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 15:14\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.15.14\">14</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 23:2\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.23.2\">23:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 24:6\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.24.6\">24:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 24:31\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.24.31\">31</a> + 67 times Chr.; also <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 66:21\" href=\"/Isaiah.66.21\">Is 66:21</a> (according to Vrss., but dub.), <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 44:10\" href=\"/Ezekiel.44.10\">Ez 44:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 45:5\" href=\"/Ezekiel.45.5\">45:5</a> (cf. v <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 45:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.45.4\">4</a>), <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 48:11\" href=\"/Ezekiel.48.11\">48:11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 48:12\" href=\"/Ezekiel.48.12\">12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 48:13\" href=\"/Ezekiel.48.13\">13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 48:22\" href=\"/Ezekiel.48.22\">22</a>. <strong>b.</strong>  as porters, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 9:26\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.9.26\">1 Ch 9:26</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 26:17\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.26.17\">26:17</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 34:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.34.9\">34:9</a>; 